# Quiz take UI (Connect Over / Discover)

Use `apps/mobile/quizzes/discover/_shared/QuizTakeShell.tsx` (+ `QuizOptionTile`). Bursts use shared `HobbyEmojiBurst` (same as hobbies / onboarding).

## Hard rules

1. **Congruent rows** — same radius checkbox+label tiles (not wildly different fun shapes, not big in-tile emoji).
2. **Selected** — full accent fill on the row + checkbox colored in with a tick. Color is the main signal; no floating check badge.
3. **Emoji burst** — option emoji launches from the tap via `HobbyEmojiBurst` (power boom), arcs up, then falls all the way off the bottom of the page. Respect Reduce Motion.
4. **Always-on type box** — focused by default on take; typing and tapping options both work. No "Add a note" toggle.
5. **Advance** — mobile: Return / → on the type box. Desktop (web): Continue button. No `1/2` page chrome.
6. **Tight spacing** — compact option gap; avoid huge empty mid-screen voids.
7. **Analytics** — option id only; never note text. `take.next` still fires for → / Continue / Return advance.
8. **Accessibility** — checkbox role + checked state; Return hint; → has a label.

Do not revive the note chip, page dots, or giant emoji-in-tile grid without an explicit product ask.
